  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "On February 24, 2026, Cook expressed cautious long-run optimism that AI-driven innovation would improve people's lives. She described AI as capable of boosting productivity through faster idea creation and broadening participation in invention and entrepreneurship. On September 28, 2026, Cook described herself as a longstanding advocate of responsible AI development and said specific government roles in AI's trajectory were for elected officials to decide.",
